  "notes": "West leads the ♣10 against 6♠. After the defense takes the ♣A and returns the suit, South should draw trump and try to dispose of his 2 diamond losers.\n\nDummy's ♥A and ♥K will provide 1 discard for a diamond loser. South could take the diamond finesse to try to eliminate the other loser. It costs nothing, however, to trump one of dummy's hearts first. When the ♥Q and ♥J both appear, North's ♥10 is high and South's careful play is rewarded.\n\nSouth can cross to the ♦A, spurning the finesse, and discard his remaining diamond loser on a good heart in the dummy.\n\nNotice that it is wrong to ruff a heart before cashing both the ♥A and ♥K. When South eventually leads a diamond towards dummy, he will not know if he should finesse as he will not know if dummy's hearts are running.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♣10 against 6♠. After the defense takes the ♣A and returns the suit, South should draw trump and try to dispose of his 2 diamond losers.",
    "Dummy's ♥A and ♥K will provide 1 discard for a diamond loser. South could take the diamond finesse to try to eliminate the other loser. It costs nothing, however, to trump one of dummy's hearts first. When the ♥Q and ♥J both appear, North's ♥10 is high and South's careful play is rewarded.",
    "South can cross to the ♦A, spurning the finesse, and discard his remaining diamond loser on a good heart in the dummy.",
    "Notice that it is wrong to ruff a heart before cashing both the ♥A and ♥K. When South eventually leads a diamond towards dummy, he will not know if he should finesse as he will not know if dummy's hearts are running."
  ],
